- The boundary_contract marker and in-process loaders are the test-side adjudication;
  this staged probe makes new direct crossings visible.
- 'False positives: legitimate protocol/exit-code tests and wrappers may still need
  a marker; marker reasons declare intent but are not proof and can be abused.'
- 'False negatives: dynamic commands, aliases not statically visible, helper indirection,
  fixture builders, unparseable files, and calls outside added/modified hunk lines
  are deliberately not inferred.'
- 'Git cost: one batched staged diff query plus one git cat-file --batch query, never
  one Git process per test file.'
